    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0426" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg376"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Dun.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 137.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information and
                    the files of the legation copy of a dispatch of the 30th ultimo,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d376-f1"/> sent to Mr. Denby, United States minister at Peking, in
                    regard to the arrest of two Japanese spies at Shanghai and their delivery into
                    the custody of the Chinese authorities.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
